   "evidence": "Line 392: `let \u03c1 : SpinDensityC := \u27e8vecMulVec v (star v), posSemidef_vecMulVec_self_star v\u27e9` is local to the proof; roadmap README.md lines 626-629 list both explicit objects as deliverables.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/ComplexSpinDensity.lean",
   "fix": "Expose the witness as a named `def` (e.g. `sofferSaturating : SpinDensityC := \u27e8vecMulVec ![1,0,0,-I] (star _), posSemidef_vecMulVec_self_star _\u27e9`) with `@[simp] transversity_sofferSaturating : transversity _ = I`, `not_isTimeReversalInvariant_sofferSaturating`, and `two_mul_norm_transversity_sofferSaturating : 2 * \u2016_\u2016 = f1 _ + deltaQ _`; keep the existential as a one-line corollary if desired.",
   "issue": "The roadmap's Examples ask for an explicit non-T-invariant `SpinDensityC` and an explicit rank-one matrix saturating the Soffer bound. Both are packaged only as `exists_not_isTimeReversalInvariant`, so the witness `vecMulVec v (star v)` is unreachable by any consumer (e.g. the \u00a71.4 saturation example) and its properties cannot be used without re-proving them.",
   "line": 388
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Lines 291-307: `f1_toSpinDensity` and `g1_toSpinDensity` are stated on the bare real values, but the `h1` analogue exists only in coerced form; `h1 (toSpinDensity \u03c1 h) = (\u03c1.mat idxPP idxMM).re` holds by `rfl` via `mat_toSpinDensity`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/ComplexSpinDensity.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] lemma h1_toSpinDensity (h : \u03c1.IsTimeReversalInvariant) : PDF.h1 (\u03c1.toSpinDensity h) = \u03c1.transversity.re := rfl` alongside the existing `f1_toSpinDensity`/`g1_toSpinDensity`, and derive `ofReal_h1_toSpinDensity` from it.",
   "issue": "The only `h1` compatibility lemma for `toSpinDensity` is `ofReal_h1_toSpinDensity`, whose LHS is the coercion `((h1 (toSpinDensity \u03c1 h) : \u211d) : \u2102)`. A goal containing the bare real `h1 (\u03c1.toSpinDensity h)` (the form the roadmap's 'commutes with h1' needs and the form `f1_toSpinDensity`/`g1_toSpinDensity` use) has no simp lemma to fire and forces the consumer to unfold `h1_def` and `mat_toSpinDensity`.",
